IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III, sections 19, 20, 21, 21ZA, 21ZB, 21ZC and 22A -- layer 1:
-- the duty to tell a constable (outside the regulated sector), the permission to do so, and what telling does for a person
-- who has been involved in a transaction.
-- A rule here answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text says yes or no in its own words, and NOTHING where the text
-- limits a grant or a duty by its own wording ("where", "to prove that") and the case falls outside the limit.
-- "A business in the regulated sector" is Schedule 3A, which is not among the sources: it is a fact the caller states.
-- A day's being a bank holiday (and Good Friday's date) comes from the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971, which is not
-- among the sources either: the caller supplies the list of those days for the part of the United Kingdom concerned.

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Offences (continued)`

§§ `s 22A Meaning of employment`

-- src:421 | In sections 19 to 21B—
-- src:422 | (a) “ employment ” means any employment (whether paid or unpaid) and includes—
-- src:423 | (i) work under a contract for services or as an office-holder,
-- src:424 | (ii) work experience provided pursuant to a training course or programme or in the course of training for employment, and
-- src:425 | (iii) voluntary work;
@ref s 22A(a) (src:421-425)
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Employment facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22A(a) the work is employment` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the work`'s `any employment, whether paid or unpaid`
           OR `the work`'s `work under a contract for services or as an office-holder`
           OR `the work`'s `work experience provided pursuant to a training course or programme or in the course of training for employment`
           OR `the work`'s `voluntary work`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“employment” means any employment (whether paid or unpaid) and includes—"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:426 | (b) “employer” has a corresponding meaning.
@ref s 22A(b) (src:426)
GIVEN `the work` IS A `Employment facts`
      `the person engages the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22A(b) the person is the employer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person engages the worker` AND `s 22A(a) the work is employment` `the work` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "“employer” has a corresponding meaning"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 19 Disclosure of information: duty`

-- src:55 | (1) This section applies where a person—
-- src:56 | (a) believes or suspects that another person has committed an offence under any of sections 15 to 18, and
-- src:57 | (b) bases his belief or suspicion on information which comes to his attention—
-- src:58 | (i) in the course of a trade, profession or business, or
-- src:59 | (ii) in the course of his employment (whether or not in the course of a trade, profession or business).
@ref s 19(1) (src:55-59)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Information facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(1) this section applies to the person` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `believes or suspects that another person has committed an offence under any of sections 15 to 18`
           AND (`the facts`'s `bases the belief or suspicion on information that came in the course of a trade, profession or business`
                OR `the facts`'s `bases the belief or suspicion on information that came in the course of employment`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a person—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:60 | (1A) But this section does not apply if the information came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 19(1A) (src:60)
GIVEN `the information came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(1A) this section does not apply to the person` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But this section does not apply if the information came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:80 | (7A) The reference to a business in the regulated sector must be construed in accordance with Schedule 3A.
@ref s 19(7A) (src:80)
GIVEN `the answer Schedule 3A gives` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(7A) the business is a business in the regulated sector` IS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 3A decides what is a business in the regulated sector and is not among the sources; with no answer from it, NOTHING
    `the answer Schedule 3A gives`

-- src:61 | (2) The person commits an offence if he does not disclose to a constable as soon as is reasonably practicable—
-- src:62 | (a) his belief or suspicion, and
-- src:63 | (b) the information on which it is based.
@ref s 19(2) (src:61-63)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Information facts`
      `what the person disclosed` IS A `Disclosure facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(2) the person commits an offence by not disclosing to a constable` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But this section does not apply if the information came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector."
        IF `the facts`'s `the information came in the course of a business in the regulated sector`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person commits an offence if he does not disclose to a constable as soon as is reasonably practicable"
        IF `what the person disclosed`'s `discloses to a constable the belief or suspicion`
           AND `what the person disclosed`'s `discloses to a constable the information on which it is based`
           AND `what the person disclosed`'s `as soon as is reasonably practicable`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 19(1) this section applies to the person` `the facts`

-- src:61 | (2) The person commits an offence if he does not disclose to a constable as soon as is reasonably practicable—
-- src:62 | (a) his belief or suspicion, and
-- src:63 | (b) the information on which it is based.
@ref s 19(2) (src:61-63)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 19(2) the person must disclose to a constable` IS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `disclose the belief or suspicion and the information to a constable`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 19(2): the person did not disclose his belief or suspicion, and the information on which it is based, to a constable as soon as is reasonably practicable"

-- src:64 | (3) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (2) to prove that he had a reasonable excuse for not making the disclosure.
@ref s 19(3) (src:64)
GIVEN `charged with an offence under s 19(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proves that he had a reasonable excuse for not making the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- JUST FALSE here means only: this section gives no defence on these facts.
-- It does not say the person has no defence at all, because another provision (s 18(2), s 19(4), s 21(5), s 21ZC) may still give one.
DECIDE `s 19(3) the person has a defence` IS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person charged with an offence under subsection (2)" (a person not so charged is outside the grant: a scope limit with no "only", ruling of 2026-11-05, (c); assumed, not ruled, that this limb is a scope limit and not part of the proof, fork F18)
        IF (NOT `charged with an offence under s 19(2)`)
            THEN NOTHING
        IF `proves that he had a reasonable excuse for not making the disclosure`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (2) to prove that he had a reasonable excuse" (the proof is not made: ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); this section gives no defence on these facts)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:65 | (4) Where—
-- src:66 | (a) a person is in employment,
-- src:67 | (b) his employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures of the matters specified in subsection (2), and
-- src:68 | (c) he is charged with an offence under that subsection,
-- src:69 | it is a defence for him to prove that he disclosed the matters specified in that subsection in accordance with the procedure.
@ref s 19(4) (src:65-69)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Procedure facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- JUST FALSE here means only: this section gives no defence on these facts.
-- It does not say the person has no defence at all, because another provision (s 18(2), s 19(3), s 21(5), s 21ZC) may still give one.
DECIDE `s 19(4) the person has a defence` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the person is in employment`
           AND `the facts`'s `the employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures`
           AND `the facts`'s `the person is charged with the offence`
           AND `the facts`'s `the person disclosed in accordance with the procedure`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a person is in employment, (b) his employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures of the matters specified in subsection (2), and (c) he is charged with an offence under that subsection," (a "where" condition that is not met: ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
        IF (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is in employment`)
           OR (NOT `the facts`'s `the employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures`)
           OR (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is charged with the offence`)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for him to prove that he disclosed the matters specified in that subsection in accordance with the procedure" (the "where" conditions hold and the proof is not made: ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); this section gives no defence on these facts)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:73 | (6) For the purpose of subsection (5) information is obtained by an adviser in privileged circumstances if it comes to him, otherwise than with a view to furthering a criminal purpose—
-- src:74 | (a) from a client or a client’s representative, in connection with the provision of legal advice by the adviser to the client,
-- src:75 | (b) from a person seeking legal advice from the adviser, or from the person’s representative, or
-- src:76 | (c) from any person, for the purpose of actual or contemplated legal proceedings.
@ref s 19(6) (src:73-76)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Privilege facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(6) the information is obtained by the adviser in privileged circumstances` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `it came otherwise than with a view to furthering a criminal purpose`
           AND (`the facts`'s `it came from a client or a client's representative in connection with the provision of legal advice by the adviser to the client`
                OR `the facts`'s `it came from a person seeking legal advice from the adviser, or from the person's representative`
                OR `the facts`'s `it came from any person for the purpose of actual or contemplated legal proceedings`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "information is obtained by an adviser in privileged circumstances if it comes to him, otherwise than with a view to furthering a criminal purpose"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:70 | (5) Subsection (2) does not require disclosure by a professional legal adviser of—
-- src:71 | (a) information which he obtains in privileged circumstances, or
-- src:72 | (b) a belief or suspicion based on information which he obtains in privileged circumstances.
@ref s 19(5) (src:70-72)
GIVEN `the person is a professional legal adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was obtained in privileged circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the belief or suspicion is based on information obtained in privileged circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(5) subsection (2) requires the professional legal adviser to disclose` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a professional legal adviser`
           AND (`the information was obtained in privileged circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                OR `the belief or suspicion is based on information obtained in privileged circumstances` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by a professional legal adviser of— (a) information which he obtains in privileged circumstances" (outside the adviser's privileged information the subsection says nothing)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:77 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a) a person shall be treated as having committed an offence under one of sections 15 to 18 if—
-- src:78 | (a) he has taken an action or been in possession of a thing, and
-- src:79 | (b) he would have committed an offence under one of those sections if he had been in the United Kingdom at the time when he took the action or was in possession of the thing.
@ref s 19(7) (src:77-79)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Act abroad facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(7) the person is treated as having committed an offence under one of sections 15 to 18` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the person has taken an action or been in possession of a thing`
           AND `the facts`'s `the person would have committed an offence under one of sections 15 to 18 if in the United Kingdom at the time`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person shall be treated as having committed an offence under one of sections 15 to 18 if"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:81 | (7B) The reference to a constable includes a reference to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of this section by the Director General of that Agency.
@ref s 19(7B) (src:81)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Officer facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(7B) the person is a constable for the purposes of s 19` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person`'s `a constable` OR `the person`'s `a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of the section by the Director General of that Agency`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The reference to a constable includes a reference to a National Crime Agency officer authorised"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:82 | (8) A person guilty of an offence under this section shall be liable—
-- src:83 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years, to a fine or to both, or
-- src:84 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both.
@ref s 19(8) (src:82-84)
GIVEN `the route of conviction` IS A `Conviction route`
      `the statutory maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling`
DECIDE `s 19(8) the ceiling of the penalty for an offence under s 19` IS
    CONSIDER `the route of conviction`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF (5 TIMES 12), `No ceiling is stated`
                                            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "to a fine or to both" states no ceiling for the fine
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF 6, `A fine not exceeding` `the statutory maximum`

§§ `s 20 Disclosure of information: permission`

-- src:86 | (1) A person may disclose to a constable—
-- src:87 | (a) a suspicion or belief that any money or other property is terrorist property or is derived from terrorist property;
-- src:88 | (b) any matter on which the suspicion or belief is based.
@ref s 20(1) (src:86-88)
GIVEN `the matter disclosed is a suspicion or belief that money or other property is terrorist property or is derived from terrorist property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter disclosed is a matter on which the suspicion or belief is based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(1) the person may disclose to a constable` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the matter disclosed is a suspicion or belief that money or other property is terrorist property or is derived from terrorist property`
            OR `the matter disclosed is a matter on which the suspicion or belief is based`)
           AND `the disclosure is to a constable`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may disclose to a constable—" (a disclosure of another kind, or to another person, is outside the grant)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:86 | (1) A person may disclose to a constable—
-- src:87 | (a) a suspicion or belief that any money or other property is terrorist property or is derived from terrorist property;
-- src:88 | (b) any matter on which the suspicion or belief is based.
@ref s 20(1) (src:86-88)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 20(1) the person may disclose to a constable, as a permission` IS
    PARTY `the person`
    MAY `disclose the matter to a constable`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:89 | (2) A person may make a disclosure to a constable in the circumstances mentioned in section 19(1) and (2).
@ref s 20(2) (src:89)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Information facts`
      `the disclosure is to a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(2) the person may make a disclosure to a constable in the circumstances mentioned in s 19(1) and (2)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is to a constable` AND `s 19(1) this section applies to the person` `the facts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may make a disclosure to a constable in the circumstances mentioned in section 19(1) and (2)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:90 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) shall have effect notwithstanding any restriction on the disclosure of information imposed by statute or otherwise.
@ref s 20(3) (src:90)
GIVEN `permitted by s 20(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `permitted by s 20(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(3) a restriction on disclosure imposed by statute or otherwise does not prevent the disclosure` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `permitted by s 20(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `permitted by s 20(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections (1) and (2) shall have effect notwithstanding any restriction" (a disclosure outside (1) and (2) is outside the override)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:91 | (4) Where—
-- src:92 | (a) a person is in employment, and
-- src:93 | (b) his employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures of the kinds mentioned in subsection (1) and section 19(2),
-- src:94 | subsections (1) and (2) shall have effect in relation to that person as if any reference to disclosure to a constable included a reference to disclosure in accordance with the procedure.
@ref s 20(4) (src:91-94)
GIVEN `the person is in employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures of the kinds mentioned in s 20(1) and s 19(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in accordance with the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(4) a disclosure in accordance with the employer's procedure counts as a disclosure to a constable` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is in employment`
           AND `the employer has established a procedure for the making of disclosures of the kinds mentioned in s 20(1) and s 19(2)`
           AND `the disclosure is made in accordance with the procedure`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a person is in employment, and (b) his employer has established a procedure"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:95 | (5) References to a constable include references to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of this section by the Director General of that Agency .
@ref s 20(5) (src:95)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Officer facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(5) the person is a constable for the purposes of s 20` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person`'s `a constable` OR `the person`'s `a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of the section by the Director General of that Agency`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References to a constable include references to a National Crime Agency officer authorised"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 21 Cooperation with police`

