        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement in a transaction or arrangement relating to money or other property if he discloses to a constable"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:108 | (5) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under any of sections 15(2) and (3) and 16 to 18 to prove that—
-- src:109 | (a) he intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in subsections (2) and (3), and
-- src:110 | (b) there is reasonable excuse for his failure to do so.
@ref s 21(5) (src:108-110)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Offence of Part III`
      `intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in s 21(2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is reasonable excuse for his failure to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- JUST FALSE here means only: this section gives no defence on these facts.
-- It does not say the person has no defence at all, because another provision (s 18(2), s 19(3), s 19(4), s 21ZC) may still give one.
DECIDE `s 21(5) the person has a defence` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence charged`
    WHEN `an offence under s 15(1)` THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any of sections 15(2) and (3) and 16 to 18" (section 15(1) is not named: a scope limit with no "only", ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))
        NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        -- the range "16 to 18" is read as including section 17A, which lies inside it (fork F7)
        IF `intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in s 21(2) and (3)` AND `there is reasonable excuse for his failure to do so`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under any of sections 15(2) and (3) and 16 to 18 to prove that— (a) he intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in subsections (2) and (3), and (b) there is reasonable excuse for his failure to do so" (either limb is not proved: ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); this section gives no defence on these facts)
        ELSE JUST FALSE

