        IF `a transaction or arrangement relating to money or other property` OR `the involvement is use or possession`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to use or possession"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 21ZA Arrangements with prior consent`

-- src:122 | (4) A working day is a day other than a Saturday, a Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday or a day that is a bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 (c.80) in the part of the United Kingdom in which the person is when making the disclosure.
@ref s 21ZA(4) (src:122)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the bank holidays and Good Fridays in the part of the United Kingdom where the person is` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A working day is a day other than a Saturday, a Sunday"
        IF `is weekend` day THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A working day is a day other than ... Christmas Day"
        IF DATE_DAY day EQUALS 25 AND DATE_MONTH day EQUALS 12 THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A working day is a day other than ... Good Friday or a day that is a bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971"
        IF elem day `the bank holidays and Good Fridays in the part of the United Kingdom where the person is` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:121 | (3) The notice period is the period of 7 working days starting with the first working day after the person makes the disclosure.
@ref s 21ZA(3) (src:121)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21ZA(3) the working day numbered` n `counting from` day `and` holidays MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` day holidays EQUALS JUST TRUE AND n AT MOST 1 THEN day
        IF `s 21ZA(4) the day is a working day` day holidays EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `s 21ZA(3) the working day numbered` (n MINUS 1) `counting from` (day PLUS 1) `and` holidays
        OTHERWISE `s 21ZA(3) the working day numbered` n `counting from` (day PLUS 1) `and` holidays

-- src:121 | (3) The notice period is the period of 7 working days starting with the first working day after the person makes the disclosure.
@ref s 21ZA(3) (src:121)
GIVEN `the day the disclosure is made` IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` MEANS
    `s 21ZA(3) the working day numbered` 7 `counting from` (`the day the disclosure is made` PLUS 1) `and` holidays

-- src:120 | (2) A person is treated as having an authorised officer's consent if before the end of the notice period the person does not receive notice from an authorised officer that consent is refused.
@ref s 21ZA(2) (src:120)
GIVEN `the day the disclosure is made` IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day notice that consent is refused was received` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21ZA(2) the person is treated as having the authorised officer's consent` IS
    CONSIDER `the day notice that consent is refused was received`
    WHEN JUST received THEN
        IF received AT LEAST `the day the disclosure is made` AND received AT MOST `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` `the day the disclosure is made` holidays
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an authorised officer's consent if before the end of the notice period the person does not receive notice"
            JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day I am asking about` GREATER THAN `s 21ZA(3) the last day of the notice period` `the day the disclosure is made` holidays
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an authorised officer's consent if before the end of the notice period the person does not receive notice" (the period has not yet ended, so the "if" is not met: ruling of 2026-11-05, (a); fork F3)
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:117 | (1) A person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement in a transaction or an arrangement relating to money or other property if, before becoming involved, the person—
-- src:118 | (a) discloses to an authorised officer the person's suspicion or belief that the money or other property is terrorist property and the information on which the suspicion or belief is based, and
-- src:119 | (b) has the authorised officer's consent to becoming involved in the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 21ZA(1) (src:117-119)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Prior consent facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21ZA(1) the person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement, having disclosed first and had consent` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `involved in a transaction or an arrangement relating to money or other property`
           AND `the facts`'s `before becoming involved, discloses to an authorised officer the suspicion or belief that the money or other property is terrorist property and the information on which it is based`
           AND `the facts`'s `has the authorised officer's consent to becoming involved`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person does not commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 by involvement in a transaction or an arrangement relating to money or other property if, before becoming involved"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

