§§ `s 21ZB Disclosure after entering into arrangements`

-- src:129 | (2) This section applies only where—
-- src:130 | (a) there is a reasonable excuse for the person's failure to make the disclosure before becoming involved in the transaction or arrangement, and
-- src:131 | (b) the disclosure is made on the person's own initiative and as soon as it is reasonably practicable for the person to make it.
@ref s 21ZB(2) (src:129-131)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Later disclosure facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21ZB(2) section 21ZB applies to the person` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `reasonable excuse for the failure to make the disclosure before becoming involved`
           AND `the facts`'s `the disclosure is made on the person's own initiative`
           AND `the facts`'s `the disclosure is made as soon as it is reasonably practicable`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only where"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

