§§ `s 21ZC Reasonable excuse for failure to disclose`

-- src:138 | It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 to prove that—
-- src:139 | (a) the person intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in section 21ZA or 21ZB, and
-- src:140 | (b) there is a reasonable excuse for the person's failure to do so.
@ref s 21ZC (src:138-140)
GIVEN `charged with an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in s 21ZA or s 21ZB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a reasonable excuse for the failure to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- JUST FALSE here means only: this section gives no defence on these facts.
-- It does not say the person has no defence at all, because another provision (s 18(2), s 19(3), s 19(4), s 21(5)) may still give one.
DECIDE `s 21ZC the person has a defence` IS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person charged with an offence under any of sections 15 to 18" (a person not so charged is outside the grant: a scope limit with no "only", ruling of 2026-11-05, (c); assumed, not ruled, that this limb is a scope limit and not part of the proof, fork F18)
        IF (NOT `charged with an offence under any of sections 15 to 18`)
            THEN NOTHING
        IF `intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in s 21ZA or s 21ZB`
           AND `there is a reasonable excuse for the failure to do so`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 to prove that— (a) the person intended to make a disclosure of the kind mentioned in section 21ZA or 21ZB, and (b) there is a reasonable excuse for the person's failure to do so" (either limb is not proved: ruling of 2026-11-05, (b); this section gives no defence on these facts)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
